    "question": {
      "math_academy_id": "q-140592",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Which of the following shaded areas describes the region bounded by the inequality $y>-x-1?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we draw the corresponding straight line $y=-x-1.$ Since the inequality involves a 'strictly greater than' sign, the line $y=-x-1$ itself is *not* part of the solution. Therefore, we draw a **dashed line.** \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/786edd428c1bea9a8a9003050a9a044491c256cb7aa9f3c189eba3b94d0a4ab3.png)\n\nThen, we must decide whether to shade above or below the line. The inequality $y>-x-1$ refers to the $y$-values that are *greater than* those on the line $y=-x-1,$ so we shade *above* the line. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/406d6b56a5aa29b34ca31515e3b7c291a55a2f1df6be69672fe824fdc0e672f6.png)\n\n \n\nLet's now check that we've shaded the correct part. First, we consider a point in the shaded region, say $(0,1).$  \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14274623/assets/65472f4ca46be1f2f7093d06e8b08c16ce934a54df4823a14f74cd5cd34ad945.png)\n\nWhen we substitute the coordinates of this point into our inequality, we get a true statement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & >-x-1 \\\\ (1) & >-(0)-1 \\\\ 1 & >-1\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis indicates that we have shaded the correct region.",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
      "result": "Correct",
      "grade": "Correct",
      "source_grade": "Correct",
